spice-widget: show a part of the display (seamless app windows)

WinBoat's seamless mode shows each window of a Windows app in a Linux window of its own, like RDP's RemoteApp: every
window is a SpiceDisplay of the same display channel that shows only that window's rectangle. Add
spice_display_set_window_area(), which replaces the monitor's area with the given one (drawing, size and input),
and send pointer positions for the whole display from such a widget (also outside it, clamped to the display:
dragging the guest window by its title bar leaves the widget).

Several widgets then draw every gl-draw, and each acknowledged it: the server counts one acknowledgement per client.
Send one GL_DRAW_DONE per gl-draw.

